- No `onEvict` provided, or non-function – no crash
- `set()` overwrite must not trigger hook; internal delete must bypass hook
- Capacity loop may evict multiple entries, each with `capacity` reason
- `clear()` must snapshot entries to preserve oldest-first order and call hook after removal
- Hook throwing should not corrupt LRU state (call after delete)
- SessionStore rehydration may itself cause another capacity eviction → chained save
- Destroyed id must not be saved even if `delete()` triggers hook – only save on `capacity`
