The cursor must encode the last seen position (`createdAt`, `id`) to provide stable ordering when `createdAt` duplicates and new rows are inserted. An empty string denotes the first page, otherwise the cursor is decoded with the provided helpers and validated; any failure maps to `invalid cursor`. Mutual presence of `page` and `cursor` is rejected. For cursor mode the sorted list is scanned for the first row strictly less than the cursor in `(createdAt desc, id desc)` order, sliced by `pageSize`, and `nextCursor` is `null` when no rows remain, including an exactly full last page. Offset mode is left byte-for-byte identical to preserve legacy clients.

